1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:06,875
A hard decision can be difficult to explain,
and harder to share before you are ready.

2
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:12,761
Harmonise starts privately and leaves peer
connection up to you.

3
00:00:13,261 --> 00:00:24,145
It is for people facing personal decisions,
family pressure, or life changes. This is peer
support, not therapy.

4
00:00:24,645 --> 00:00:34,466
We sign in with the shared demo account.
Community names and counts are real; member
stories stay private.

5
00:00:34,966 --> 00:00:39,619
The member describes pressure to decide for
their family.

6
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:47,557
Muse Wonder offers a live reflection and
practical options, with Muse Spark as
fallback.

7
00:00:48,057 --> 00:00:55,344
The app names the model that answered. Matches
appear only when the member asks.

8
00:00:55,844 --> 00:01:04,620
Private advice is not copied into a peer
space. The public directory comes from
Supabase.

9
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:11,725
When no circle fits, Meta drafts a possible
scope from the member's idea.

10
00:01:12,225 --> 00:01:20,173
The member can edit or discard the draft. A
human reviews any proposal before launch.

11
00:01:20,673 --> 00:01:27,043
Muse Voice Transcribe turns speech into text
the member can review and edit.

12
00:01:27,543 --> 00:01:33,126
That transcript stays unsent until the member
chooses what to do.

13
00:01:33,626 --> 00:01:45,604
Muse Spark also supports chat, community
guidance, and advisory moderation triage.
People make consequential decisions.

14
00:01:46,104 --> 00:01:54,361
Next.js, Supabase Auth and Postgres, and
server-side Meta models connect the journey.

15
00:01:54,861 --> 00:02:04,093
We aim to make a first step easier to see and
connection easier to choose. We have not
measured outcomes.
